# O10-CONTROL acceptance (author-owned). Every check must pass once the outcome is implemented.
# Written on main e45d947, where 43 of these 63 fail by design (evidence-o10c-acceptance/main-run.log).
# The passing ones are regression guards: 2.4.0 registry/state/socket compatibility, quiet/resume, and
# failures that already show on their layer.
N2a from idle, a room that fails shows the failure card on Now named after the target, with Try again and Back
N2b ... and the window never went back to Rooms while it failed
N2c ... and nothing was left playing (the idle state is intact)
N2d Try again sends one enter for the same room and, with the fault gone, that room plays
N2e Back from that card returns to Rooms and the card is gone, still with nothing playing
# Phase 2: N2f-h and N2k now start the playing room as a catalogue room (Midnight library); the station room
# took the target's name after an earlier scenario entered it, so no enter was sent. N2f0/N2k0 guard that.
N2f0 (setup) the playing room is not the target and the window sent an enter for the target
N2f while another room plays, a room that fails shows the failure card named after the target (not the playing room), with Try again and Back
N2g ... and the previous room is intact: same room, same layers, still playing
N2h Back keeps the previous room playing and the card goes away
N2i a room whose music alone fails is entered: its ambience plays
N2j ... the window stays on Now and the failure shows on the music layer
N2k0 (setup) the playing room is not Rainy quiet and the window sent an enter for it
# Coordinator decision (phase 2): a music-only failure while another room plays keeps that room intact and shows
# the target card (o6 7n/7o win over entering a half-working room). N2k is superseded by N2m-o; kept as known.
!N2k [ORIGINAL, superseded by N2m-o] while another room plays, a room whose music alone fails is entered with its ambience playing, on Now, with the music failure shown
N2m while another room plays, a room whose music alone fails shows the failure card named after it, with Try again and Back, and it stays
N2n ... and the playing room is intact: same room, same layers, still playing (the new ambience never started)
N2o ... and Back keeps the playing room playing and the card goes away
N2l a music change that fails inside a playing room shows on the music layer; the ambience keeps playing and the window stays on Now without a room failure card
E0 (reference) the window's room Pause pauses music and ambience and keeps the scene
E1 MPRIS reports Playing for a playing room
E2 MPRIS Pause pauses the room exactly as the window's Pause does (music and ambience paused, scene kept)
E3 ... and MPRIS then reports Paused
E4 the window's Play resumes a room MPRIS paused: everything that played plays again
E5 MPRIS Play resumes a room the window paused, exactly as it was
E6 MPRIS PlayPause on a playing room pauses it like the window's Pause
E7 ... and PlayPause again restores exactly what played
E7b MPRIS PlayPause on a room the window paused restores exactly what played
E8 with only the ambience playing (music paused on its own), MPRIS still reports the room as Playing
E9 ... and MPRIS Pause silences it: the ambience pauses too
E10 with the music stopped and the ambience playing, MPRIS reports Playing and Pause pauses the ambience
# E11 sampled 0.9 s after MPRIS Stop; a Stop that runs the faded Leave (1.2 s, like the window's Leave) is
# not a failure. Superseded by E11b (phase 2, 423dd3a); kept as a known failure.
!E11 [ORIGINAL, superseded by E11b] MPRIS Stop stops the room: nothing is left audible
E11b MPRIS Stop stops the room: within 5 s (a Leave fade) nothing is left audible
E12 MPRIS metadata names the room
E13 ... and what plays (the music's station or track)
E14 with only the ambience playing, MPRIS metadata names the room and the ambience
E15 the media key (listening-hub toggle) pauses the whole room exactly as the window's Pause does
E16 ... and the window then offers Play/Resume for the room
E17 the media key on a room the window paused restores exactly what played
E18 with only the ambience still playing, the media key silences the room
L1 the Mix has a visible control (not in a menu) for music pause that touches only that layer
L2 the Mix has a visible control (not in a menu) for music resume that touches only that layer
L3 the Mix has a visible control (not in a menu) for music stop that touches only that layer
L4 the Mix has a visible control (not in a menu) for ambience pause that touches only that layer
L5 the Mix has a visible control (not in a menu) for ambience resume that touches only that layer
L6 the Mix has a visible control (not in a menu) for ambience stop that touches only that layer
L7 with the music paused on its own, room Pause silences everything and room Resume restores exactly what played (ambience back, music still paused)
L8 room Pause then Resume with everything playing restores everything
L9 Play on a room silent because every layer was paused on its own starts sound again
L10 ... and MPRIS Play and listening-roomctl resume do the same as the window's Play
N9a (setup) the cold-start Connecting state was observed on Now
N9b connecting to a radio room from a cold start shows no track controls (Next track, Less/More like this)
N9c ... and never shows the volume at 0 while the stored room volume is 70 (a shown level is 70)
N9d (setup) the library room shows Next track before switching
N9f (setup) the Connecting state from the library room was observed on Now
N9e connecting from a library room to a radio room hides the previous room's track controls
N10 (radio-and-rain) no menu on Now or in the Mix holds a single item
N10 (radio-only) no menu on Now or in the Mix holds a single item
N10 (music-failed) no menu on Now or in the Mix holds a single item
N10 (library) no menu on Now or in the Mix holds a single item
C6a every 2.4.0 controller action still exists with the same argument types (changes are additive)
C6b ... and what ran at once still runs at once (quiet, resume, stop, layer pause/stop)
C6c the snapshot keeps every 2.4.0 field
C6d a 2.4.0 client over the socket: layer pause/play act on that layer; quiet pauses the room with a resume offer and resume restores it
C6e session state stored by 2.4.0 loads unchanged and its room can be returned to
C6f listening-roomctl pauses the music layer alone
C6g listening-roomctl pauses the ambience layer alone
C6h ... and resumes and stops each layer alone (the other layer keeps playing)
C6i listening-roomctl --help lists the layer action
# C6j wanted the literal `listening-roomctl WORD`; a usage line `listening-roomctl music|ambience ...` documents
# the same command. Superseded by C6j2 (phase 2, 423dd3a); kept as a known failure.
!C6j [ORIGINAL, superseded by C6j2] the session runbook documents the roomctl layer command
C6j2 the session runbook documents the roomctl layer command (literally or as a usage line)
C6k the CHANGELOG records the change above 2.4.0: MPRIS/media keys act on the room, and roomctl layer actions
